# Umami analytics, served first-party.
#
# This rule must stay ABOVE the SPA catch-all: Netlify matches _redirects top to
# bottom and the first match wins, so /* would otherwise swallow it and hand back
# index.html.
#
# It exists so the tracker loads from consolelogic.net instead of umami.is,
# which EasyPrivacy blocks by hostname (||umami.is^$third-party). Unproxied,
# that silently drops every visitor running a content blocker, which is a large
# share of a developer audience.
#
# Only the script is proxied here. The collect endpoint (/api/send, a path the
# tracker fixes and we cannot rename) is handled by the edge function in
# netlify/edge-functions/umami-collect.js instead, because it has to forward
# the visitor's real IP and a plain rewrite cannot add a header.
/js/stats.js  https://cloud.umami.is/script.js    200

# SPA fallback. Prerendered routes are real files in dist, and Netlify serves an
# existing file ahead of an unforced rewrite, so this only catches unknown paths.
/*  /index.html  200
